I go to my window.
I hold my phone up.
"Look," I say.
"This is Copenhagen."
Outside, it is dark.
It is evening in Denmark.
But there are many lights from the city.
I think it is beautiful.
My mother looks at the screen.
"Oh, Maya," she says.
"It is so dark there!"
I smile.
In Mexico, it is light now.
It is afternoon there.
